{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "795039eb-0806-5a7e-932b-a48e187542f2",
    "name": "SpaceMatch Reel Analytics API",
    "description": "Hub API (`/v1`) for SpaceMatch Reel Analytics.\n\n**Start here:** select the *SpaceMatch Reels - Local* (or *Render*) environment, then run folder **0. Setup** once. It logs in to the dashboard as an agent and creates that agent's API key, saved to `apiKey`. Every `/v1` request sends it as `Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}` (set on the collection).\n\nIDs chain automatically: *Create property* saves `propertyId`, *Add a link* saves `linkId`, refreshes save `refreshId`. Dashboard (`/api/...`) requests fetch a fresh CSRF token automatically (collection pre-request script).\n\nFull reference: `{{baseUrl}}/api/docs`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{apiKey}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Dashboard routes (/api/...) need a CSRF token that matches the session cookie.",
          "// Fetch a fresh one before every non-GET dashboard request, so it never goes stale",
          "// (switching baseUrl, redeploys, logging in all start a new session).",
          "const path = pm.request.url.getPath();",
          "// /v1 requests authenticate with the API key only (not the login session).",
          "if (path.startsWith('/v1/') && !path.startsWith('/v1/health') && !pm.environment.get('apiKey')) {",
          "  throw new Error('apiKey is empty - run \"0. Setup > Create API key\" first (logging in clears the old key).');",
          "}",
          "if (pm.request.method !== 'GET' && path.startsWith('/api/')) {",
          "  pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.environment.get('baseUrl') + '/api/me', method: 'GET' }, (err, res) => {",
          "    if (err || res.code !== 200) { console.warn('Could not refresh CSRF token', err || res.code); return; }",
          "    pm.environment.set('csrf', res.json().csrf);",
          "  });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup (dashboard login + API key)",
      "description": "Run these once per agent. They use the dashboard session (cookie + CSRF), not the API key.\n\n1. **Sign up agent** creates the agent in `agentEmail` (a 409 means it already exists - fine).\n2. **Log in agent** - also clears the previous `apiKey`, so a key from another agent is never reused.\n3. **Create API key** stores the new secret in `apiKey`.\n\n**The API key decides whose data `/v1` touches.** Properties created with it belong to the agent who created the key - the agent you logged in as in step 2. Switching agents? Log in and create a key again.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get CSRF token",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Optional - every dashboard request fetches a fresh token itself."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));",
                  "pm.environment.set('csrf', pm.response.json().csrf);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign up agent",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-CSRF-Token",
                "value": "{{csrf}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "signup"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates an agent account. 409 = already registered (continue with Log in).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"{{agentName}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{agentEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{agentPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is one of [200, 409]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 409]));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) pm.environment.set('csrf', pm.response.json().csrf);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in agent",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-CSRF-Token",
                "value": "{{csrf}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{agentEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{agentPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));",
                  "pm.environment.set('csrf', pm.response.json().csrf);",
                  "// A key belongs to one agent: drop the old one so the next /v1 calls can't act as someone else.",
                  "pm.environment.unset('apiKey'); pm.environment.unset('apiKeyId'); pm.environment.unset('propertyId'); pm.environment.unset('linkId');",
                  "pm.test('Logged in as agent', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().user.role).to.equal('agent'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create API key",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-CSRF-Token",
                "value": "{{csrf}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/api-keys",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "api-keys"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The secret is returned only here. It is saved to the `apiKey` environment variable.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman\",\n  \"scopes\": [\n    \"properties:read\",\n    \"properties:write\",\n    \"socials:read\",\n    \"socials:write\",\n    \"refresh:write\",\n    \"logs:read\"\n  ],\n  \"environment\": \"production\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));",
                  "const k = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.environment.set('apiKey', k.secret);",
                  "pm.environment.set('apiKeyId', k.id);",
                  "pm.test('Secret returned once', () => pm.expect(k.secret).to.include('sk_'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List API keys",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/api-keys",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "api-keys"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Secrets are never listed, only the prefix."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));",
                  "pm.test('No secrets in the list', () => pm.expect(JSON.stringify(pm.response.json())).to.not.include(pm.environment.get('apiKey')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "auth": {
        "type": "noauth"
      }
    },
